+## Follow-up — raster call graph and probe idle behavior (2026-10-17)
+
+- A fresh repository-wide call-site search found no editor consumer of
+  `nativeRasterFrame` or `nativeRasterPlan`. `native_raster_frame` is registered
+  as a Tauri command and the TypeScript client exposes it, but the editor does
+  not call it; returned pixels are not currently displayed through Canvas2D
+  either. The earlier wording that native RGBA reaches the Canvas2D surface
+  was therefore too strong. `docs/architecture/native-render-stage.md` now
+  describes the command as an offscreen raster API with no current display
+  consumer. The feature page and performance guide remain truthful and need no
+  native-presentation marketing claim or copy change.
+- The real Tauri probe uses `GtkGLArea` as the `GtkOverlay` base child and keeps
+  the Wry WebView in front. The home-view capture showed the marker hidden by
+  the opaque page. The editor's `.editor-canvas` background and canvas render
+  routines also paint opaque surface pixels, so this layout cannot yet reveal
+  native document pixels. The next integration slice must establish a native
+  frame consumer, match the editor canvas rectangle and viewport generation,
+  and complete the transparent-region/Canvas2D handoff without exposing stale
+  or double-rendered pixels. Input and a real-document editor screenshot are
+  still pending.
+- The static diagnostic now disables `GtkGLArea` auto-render; attach queues one
+  initial draw, and future frame updates must explicitly queue a replacement.
+  This avoids continuously redrawing a marker that never changes.
+- `9c5adfca2` corrects the native-render guide's call-graph claims. Its staged
+  plan and affected run pass (`audit:emoji`, `audit:docs`; 1,166 docs, 864
+  links, 182 ADRs in the isolated checkout). `7abf26beb` disables idle GLArea
+  auto-render. Direct `rustfmt --check --edition 2021` passes for the changed
+  presenter file. Workspace `cargo fmt --check` reports unrelated format
+  drift in `collab_host.rs`, `lib.rs`, and `lifecycle.rs`.
+- The isolated worktree's first `pnpm verify:affected --staged` stopped at the
+  pre-existing `audit:radius` failure (10 raw-radius consumers in Presentation
+  and SpecPanel CSS). The presenter change's next affected run stopped at
+  desktop TypeScript before package units/native lanes because this clean
+  branch lacks the root worktree's uncommitted `packages/codegen/src/bundle-assets.ts`
+  and `packages/scene/src/nodeResize.ts`; it also reports the existing
+  `CollabSurfaces.tsx:450` readonly-cast issue and an `exportService.ts`
+  implicit-any error. No unrelated files were copied or modified to hide these
+  failures.
+- `cargo check --locked` initially refused the isolated checkout because its
+  committed lock predates five workspace dependency entries already present
+  in the root worktree's uncommitted `Cargo.lock`. The offline desktop check
+  (`cargo check --offline --manifest-path apps/desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml`,
+  with `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2`) then passed in 8m24s; its generated lock matched
+  the root's in-progress lock exactly and was restored in this worktree, not
+  committed. Re-run the canonical locked check after those shared dependency
+  changes are integrated.
